Package: sisura-hardening
Version: 0.3.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Sisura Maintainers <packages@sisura.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: apparmor, ufw, nftables, openssh-server, sudo, procps, kmod, passwd,
 init-system-helpers, unattended-upgrades, libpam-runtime, libpam-modules,
 libpam-pwquality, cracklib-runtime
Description: Sisura Linux security hardening
 Baseline hardening for Sisura Linux:
  - kernel sysctl hardening (info leaks, eBPF, ptrace, ASLR, network stack)
  - blacklist of rarely used / historically vulnerable kernel modules
  - key-only OpenSSH with modern crypto, per-machine host keys
  - default-deny UFW policy applied on first boot
  - nftables filter dropping IPv4 TCP packets with IP options
  - automatic installation of Debian security updates
  - removal of setuid/setgid bits outside an allowlist, re-applied after
    every dpkg run
  - sudo policy (pty, audit log, short timestamp), account lockout after
    5 failed authentications (pam_faillock), password quality (pwquality)
  - core dumps disabled, restrictive umask
